Load decks of sp_jfet2 against ngspice-45, written by ../load.py jfet2.
Builds on PATH: ngspice-45 jfngv2gd3zvi5cmr9vrqfhnziipqd09n (source hfvpfb0bgw9819wkb7kzpdaasbd0hd5r, devices/jfet2),
VACASK dhxz6l3iac3r2b8n91kcz04a0j3hs4s6 (devices/spice/jfet2.va, ngspice-47-159 vadng-pre-48).
Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/families/load_run.sh jfet2`. i(vd) in A, |i(vd)| at 1 GHz for acg/acd.
nom is 27 C, m=1, the control of m3 (27 C, m=3) and of off (80 C, m=3); all give area=2. Regions (vgs, vds) in ../load.py.
Oracles (fd.py, last lines): each nominal region's operating point moved 1e-5 V on the gate (base) and the drain
(collector, anode), whose central differences are gm and gds of the DC law, against |i(vd)| at 1 kHz; it holds where
the conductance is well above the 1 kHz capacitive current and the differences' resolution (ngspice prints 12 digits:
about 5e-11 S), so not in cutoff or reverse. And the multiplier's metamorphic relation: every m3 reading is 3 times its
nom reading within 1e-9 relative and 1e-10 absolute (the solver's gmin is not multiplied); a failing row is printed.
The Parker-Skellern model gives delta, xi, p, q, z, vbi, hfeta beside cgs and cgd.
Result: no difference. DC to 3.9e-6 (a cutoff pA), AC to 3e-13, both AC the derivatives of the DC law (1e-5).
Rechecked 2026-11-13 under R91b (../../checked.sh: a run whose exit status is not 0 or whose output says it aborted, stepped too small or met a singular matrix gives refused(<why>), never a reading): every reading reproduced.

